#. type: Title =
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/overview.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "OpenEMS: Schedule"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/overview.adoc
msgid ""
"**OpenEMS has a schedule.** It shows what the system plans for the current "
"and the next day, in quarter hours:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/overview.adoc
msgid "which **electricity price** applies,"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/overview.adoc
msgid "how much **solar yield** and **consumption** are expected,"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/overview.adoc
msgid ""
"what the **storage** should do (e.g. “delayed discharge” or “charge from "
"grid”),"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/overview.adoc
msgid "and how **grid purchase** and **state of charge** develop as a result."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/overview.adoc
msgid ""
"For past periods of the day, the schedule shows the **measured values**. "
"This way, one chart shows both what happened and what is planned."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/overview.adoc
msgid ""
"The schedule is more than the forecast: it uses the xref:user/schedule/"
"forecasts.adoc[forecasts] and shows what OpenEMS does with them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/overview.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Where to see it"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-where-to-see-it
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/overview.adoc
msgid ""
"The web interface has its own **schedule page**. Since October 2026 it "
"updates itself as soon as a new plan has been made. It also shows whether "
"planning is in progress or has been completed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/overview.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "How it is created"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-it-is-created
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/overview.adoc
msgid ""
"OpenEMS collects forecasts, electricity prices (xref:user/storage-control/"
"time-of-use-tariffs.adoc[tariffs]), the state of the storage and the grid "
"limits."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-it-is-created
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/overview.adoc
msgid ""
"An optimizer tries out many possible sequences and selects the cheapest one "
"that complies with all limits."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-it-is-created
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/overview.adoc
msgid ""
"The near future is planned in quarter hours, times further ahead in hours."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-it-is-created
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/overview.adoc
msgid ""
"The plan is renewed regularly, about every quarter of an hour, and "
"immediately when settings are changed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/overview.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "What is included in the plan"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/overview.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Function\n"
"| Role in the schedule\n"
"\n"
"| xref:user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc[Price control]\n"
"| decides when the storage is conserved, charged or discharged\n"
"| xref:user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc[Grid-optimized charge]\n"
"| delays or limits charging (together with price control)\n"
"| Charge points (wallbox)\n"
"| plan the charging of vehicles\n"
"| Heating elements (Askoma, my-PV)\n"
"| plan the heating power\n"
"| Emergency reserve, discharge limit, fixed storage power\n"
"| are taken into account as constraints for the storage\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/overview.adoc
msgid ""
"Since October 2026 the schedule is also calculated if none of these "
"controlling functions is active."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/overview.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to read the schedule"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-to-read-the-schedule
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/overview.adoc
msgid "**Past:** measured values in 5-minute steps."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-to-read-the-schedule
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/overview.adoc
msgid ""
"**Future:** plan in quarter hours. It is based on forecasts and can change "
"with each new plan."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-to-read-the-schedule
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/overview.adoc
msgid ""
"If reality differs from the forecast (e.g. clouds, unexpected consumption), "
"OpenEMS adjusts the plan the next time it plans."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-to-read-the-schedule
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/overview.adoc
msgid ""
"The period covers the current day and, as soon as available, the next one."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-to-read-the-schedule
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/overview.adoc
msgid ""
"Without electricity prices and forecasts, no meaningful schedule can be "
"created."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/overview.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "For advanced users"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-for-advanced-users
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/overview.adoc
msgid ""
"The schedule can also be retrieved via the interface, e.g. for your own "
"evaluations. This is done with the request “getSchedule” to the component "
"`+_energy+` (see xref:user/external-interfaces/json-rpc.adoc[JSON-RPC]). For "
"each quarter hour, the response contains prices, production, consumption, "
"grid, storage and state of charge, as well as the planned state of each "
"function involved."
msgstr ""
